Original commit body from 469aece998141de61daa32f9ef2e3fb756397163:

hypergumbo's own tree has both halves of the construct the WI-lubap fix
targets -- 26 argparse add_parser/set_defaults(func=) pairs in cli.py, and
scripts/hypergumbo_diag.py:960 invoking subprocess.run(["hypergumbo",
"slice", "--input", in_path, ...]) -- yet a full survey produced 0
subprocess_calls edges. The WI-lubap join was never at fault: against the
real symbol set it resolves 26/26 subcommands to 27 handlers. Three defects
sat upstream of it, the first two each sufficient alone.

B1 _detect_project_cli_name read only <root>/pyproject.toml, so any
workspace whose root manifest is tool-config-only was structurally dark --
including this one, whose `hypergumbo` script lives in
packages/hypergumbo/pyproject.toml while the root has no [project] table.
It returned an empty set, so `call.executable in project_cli_names` could
never pass and everything behind it was dead code. Now unions
[project.name], [project.scripts], setup(name=) and console_scripts across
every pyproject.toml and setup.py the shared discovery excludes admit;
setup.py is read via ast, never executed. setup.cfg stays unread -- a
declared gap.

B2 _extract_command_info literal_eval'd the WHOLE argv, so one variable
discarded the call site. Real self-invocations are almost never fully
literal. Now keeps the leading run of constants, which is exactly where the
executable and subcommand live; stopping at the first non-constant rather
than skipping it is deliberate, since positional reasoning past an opaque
element is unsound. The swallowing branch carried a no-cover pragma while
demonstrably firing on our own source; it is covered by a test now.

B3 _scan_argparse_commands indexed handlers by bare name with no kind or
path filter. On this tree 'survey' resolved to both the real cmd_run and a
same-named external_symbol whose <external> sentinel sorts before every
real path, so the INV-zuhub min-by-id tie-break actively PREFERRED the
placeholder -- fixing B1/B2 alone would have minted a confidently-wrong
edge. External placeholders are now excluded, and a same-file handler wins
over any same-named symbol elsewhere. Unlike the fire linker this falls
back to a name match rather than requiring same-file, because
`from .commands import cmd_serve` is common enough that requiring it would
trade a wrong-edge class for a recall hole.

Measured end to end on this repository, the only instrument that can see
this defect: 0 -> 4 subprocess_calls edges. Two are genuine self-invocations
the old code discarded for the same reason (a variable in the argv) --
hypergumbo_diag.py:960 -> cmd_slice at 0.85, the join WI-lubap was filed
for, and dead-code-prospector-run.py:520 -> cmd_dead_code_maybe. The other
two are subprocess.run([...]) inside string literals in the test fixture;
the scanner is regex-over-raw-text with no literal awareness, a pre-existing
gap now visible because the guard finally passes, recorded on WI-gadus as a
decision rather than folded in here.

The pre-existing test_links_subprocess_to_argparse_handler has been green
since July while the feature was dead, because its fixture defeats all three
blockers by construction: a root pyproject WITH a [project] table, a fully
literal argv, and exactly one candidate symbol. The new suite is that
scenario with each convenience removed, plus an end-to-end case with all
three at once -- 6 red-first tests, 6 pinning the fail-safe branches,
module at 100%.

